WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.630
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.180
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.840
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.770
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.430
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.510
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.700
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.650
The 
Six-Scripted 
Lantern Festival

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.120
Eat some fries!

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.120
Thanks.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.720
Did something happen?

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.890
Something?

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.880
It’s OK if you don’t want to tell me, but…

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.000
If you’re wondering about something, I could help.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.630
Thanks.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:09.280
So, let’s go home and study for exams!

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.660
How nice to have a tutor!

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.380
I should’ve been born in a rich family, too!

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.220
Are you jealous?

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.240
Well, bye bye!

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.370
See you later!

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.380
<i>Thanks, Akie.</i>

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.430
<i>Thanks to you, I can keep it up.</i>

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.320
<i>I want to talk if we can.</i>

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.380
<i>I want to say everything about me and my hardships.</i>

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:46.370
<i>Hey Akie, I have Jigoku Shoujo inside of me.</i>

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.910
<i>How long has it been since then?</i>

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.150
<i>How many have I seen so far?</i>

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:22.370
<i>When is it going to end?</i>

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.370
Hey over there!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.260
Uh oh.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.680
I wonder what you were doing?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.230
Oh, a wish?

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.120
“Exams, go away!”

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:41.010
Oh right, it’s time for the Six-Scripted Lanterns.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.190
The Six-Scripted Lanterns, eh?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:59.410
This Saigawara City is said to be the closest to Hell,

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:05.560
where during the Edo period criminals came for expiation from afar.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.600
Really?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:11.040
Knowing the feelings of those criminals,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.100
the shrine’s chief priest wrote their sins on lanterns,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:21.570
put their hair on them as a replacement, and ferried them down this river with a Six-Scripted tag.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.830
That was the start of the Six-Scripted Lanterns.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.620
Expiation, eh?

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:35.370
Although recently it’s become things wanted to be forgotten instead of sins.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:41.180
And, did you bring me here just to tell me this?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:48.040
During the ferrying of the Six-Scripted Lanterns, just for a moment, the gates of Hell are opened.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.100
Ojou can receive what’s sent to her.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:59.940
The Six-Script Lantern

